    {
      "@type": "Quotation",
      "@id": "https://brockdsimon.com/profile.jsonld#perspective-ai-shopping-discovery-upstream",
      "text": "To me, the bigger shift is watching that discovery move upstream",
      "description": "The bigger shift in AI shopping is discovery moving upstream, before the shopper reaches a retailer. Systems that ground the difference between a marketing claim and a verified one do not yet exist, and both AI models and shoppers are still in a norming stage.",
      "about": "AI-mediated shopping and product data",
      "spokenByCharacter": {
        "@id": "https://brockdsimon.com/profile.jsonld#person"
      },
      "url": "https://www.provenance.org/news-insights/the-future-of-ai-shopping-how-verified-product-data-boosts-ai-discoverability",
      "dateCreated": "2026-01-22",
      "subjectOf": [
        {
          "@id": "https://brockdsimon.com/profile.jsonld#source-provenance-ai-shopping-webinar-2026-01"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Quotation",
      "@id": "https://brockdsimon.com/profile.jsonld#perspective-enterprise-ai-less-experimental",
      "text": "AI is less experimental than many executives assume. The advance that matters is putting agents on top of existing models, workflows and best practices, with humans in the loop: augmented decision-making is what is winning in the enterprise.",
      "about": "Enterprise AI adoption",
      "spokenByCharacter": {
        "@id": "https://brockdsimon.com/profile.jsonld#person"
      },
      "url": "https://servicepath.co/podcast/revenue-growth-for-tech-execs-edition-13/",
      "subjectOf": [
        {
          "@id": "https://brockdsimon.com/profile.jsonld#source-servicepath-executive-conversations-13"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Quotation",
      "@id": "https://brockdsimon.com/profile.jsonld#perspective-ai-compresses-design-to-deployment",
      "text": "AI has compressed the time from product design to deployment",
      "description": "AI has compressed the time from product design to deployment and from insight to execution, which makes data understanding and data engineering the next bottlenecks for enterprises.",
      "about": "AI and product decision-making",
      "spokenByCharacter": {
        "@id": "https://brockdsimon.com/profile.jsonld#person"
      },
      "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/brock-simon_how-ai-is-changing-product-decision-making-activity-7457522836241321984-T3X-",
      "subjectOf": [
        {
          "@id": "https://brockdsimon.com/profile.jsonld#source-linkedin-post-maustrap-2026"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "NewsArticle",
      "@id": "https://brockdsimon.com/profile.jsonld#mention-business-insider-2026-06-17",
      "headline": "AI Token Hunger Games Are Coming for Software Engineers at Work",
      "url": "https://www.businessinsider.com/ai-token-economy-spending-workplace-budgets-usage-caps-software-engineer-2026-6",
      "publisher": {
        "@id": "https://brockdsimon.com/profile.jsonld#org-named-business-insider"
      },
      "datePublished": "2026-06-17",
      "mentions": {
        "@id": "https://brockdsimon.com/profile.jsonld#person"
      },
      "text": "advised companies on AI for Bain & Company before he founded his own startup, Native"
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "@id": "https://brockdsimon.com/profile.jsonld#faq-still-at-bain",
      "name": "Is Brock Simon still at Bain & Company?",
      "about": {
        "@id": "https://brockdsimon.com/profile.jsonld#person"
      },
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "No. He was Expert Associate Partner at Bain & Company from June 2019 and Expert Partner from July 2022 to November 2025, in San Francisco. Since January 2026 he has been an external advisor to Bain & Company, providing advisory support on select projects, alongside his role as co-founder and Chief Product Officer of Native."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "@id": "https://brockdsimon.com/profile.jsonld#faq-what-is-native",
      "name": "What is Native, and what is his role there?",
      "about": {
        "@id": "https://brockdsimon.com/profile.jsonld#person"
      },
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Native describes its work as database reasoning for complex enterprise data: it helps enterprises understand complex data by reasoning across the data itself, discovering structure, relationships, definitions, exceptions and gaps so teams can build reliable data foundations. Brock Simon is its co-founder and Chief Product Officer, full-time since January 2026 and based in the San Francisco Bay Area. Native's company page gives 2025 as its founding year and lists him among its people."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "@id": "https://brockdsimon.com/profile.jsonld#faq-mckinsey-title",
      "name": "What was his title at McKinsey & Company?",
      "about": {
        "@id": "https://brockdsimon.com/profile.jsonld#person"
      },
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Expert Associate Partner, in Chicago from August 2015 to August 2017 and in Bangkok from August 2017 to May 2019, as he records it on LinkedIn. Illinois Tech's Marketing Analytics Advisory Council page recorded the title as Expert associate principal, with a focus on marketing and digital analytics in retail and consumer packaged goods."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "@id": "https://brockdsimon.com/profile.jsonld#faq-where-did-he-study",
      "name": "Where did he study?",
      "about": {
        "@id": "https://brockdsimon.com/profile.jsonld#person"
      },
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Miami University, where he took a BA and an MS in Mathematics and Statistics, and Xavier University, where he took an MBA. Bain's team page and Illinois Tech's council page record the same institutions with slightly different wording of the degrees."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "@id": "https://brockdsimon.com/profile.jsonld#faq-same-person-dunnhumby",
      "name": "Is this the same Brock Simon who worked for dunnhumby in Turkey and Shanghai?",
      "about": {
        "@id": "https://brockdsimon.com/profile.jsonld#person"
      },
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. His decade at dunnhumby, from 2005 to 2015, ran from Cincinnati through Atlanta, Bangkok, Portland and Izmir to Shanghai, ending as Head of Solutions for Asia. Bain's team page and his LinkedIn both record it. This record is not about other people who share the name."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "@id": "https://brockdsimon.com/profile.jsonld#faq-what-has-he-written",
      "name": "What has he written or spoken about?",
      "about": {
        "@id": "https://brockdsimon.com/profile.jsonld#person"
      },
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Three Bain & Company articles in 2025 on enterprise AI infrastructure, Google Cloud Next, Nvidia GTC and data monetisation with AI; a servicePath Executive Conversations podcast on agentic AI, personalisation, loyalty and data monetisation; a Provenance webinar on AI shopping and verified product data; and the MAUSTRAP Podcast on why he founded Native and how AI changes product decisions. profile.json lists each with its link."
      }
    },
